IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-ch1-preliminary`
IMPORT `act-ch15-aids`

-- Tests for act-ch15-aids.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 15, Aids to interpretation`

§§ `Part 15.1: General`

-- s 144: "A definition in the dictionary, part 1 applies to all Acts and statutory instruments."
#ASSERT `s 144: a definition in the dictionary, part 1 applies to the thing` `an Act (including this Act)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 144: a definition in the dictionary, part 1 applies to the thing` `a statutory instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 144: a definition in the dictionary, part 1 applies to the thing` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 145 (a): "words indicating a gender include every other gender".
#ASSERT `s 145 (a): the word includes every other gender` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145 (a): the word includes every other gender` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 145 (b): "words in the singular number include the plural and words in the plural number include the singular".
#ASSERT elem `plural` (`s 145 (b): the numbers the word covers` `singular`)
#ASSERT elem `singular` (`s 145 (b): the numbers the word covers` `singular`)
#ASSERT elem `singular` (`s 145 (b): the numbers the word covers` `plural`)
#ASSERT elem `plural` (`s 145 (b): the numbers the word covers` `plural`)

-- s 146 (1): the word may, or a similar term, indicates that the function may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion.
#ASSERT `s 146 (1), (2): what the word indicates about the function` `may, or a similar term` EQUALS JUST `the function may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion`
-- s 146 (2): the word must, or a similar term, indicates that the function is required to be exercised.
#ASSERT `s 146 (1), (2): what the word indicates about the function` `must, or a similar term` EQUALS JUST `the function is required to be exercised`
-- Another word is not covered by s 146.
#ASSERT `s 146 (1), (2): what the word indicates about the function` `another word` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 147 (3) to (5): the ideas "must not be regarded as different only because different words are used or the provisions are structured in different ways".
#ASSERT `s 147 (3) to (5): the ideas in the two provisions are regarded as different` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where the difference is not only the words or the structure, the section does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 147 (3) to (5): the ideas in the two provisions are regarded as different` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 147 (6): "regard must be had to the context and history of the 2 provisions".
#ASSERT `s 147 (6): regard must be had to the context and history of the 2 provisions`
-- s 147 (7): "Subsection (6) does not limit the matters to which regard may be had."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 147 (7): subsection (6) limits the matters to which regard may be had`)

-- s 148: terms used in a statutory instrument have the meanings they have, from time to time, in the authorising law.
#ASSERT `s 148: the meaning of a term used in a statutory instrument` (JUST "the meaning in the authorising law") EQUALS JUST "the meaning in the authorising law"
#ASSERT `s 148: the meaning of a term used in a statutory instrument` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 150: "distance is to be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane".
#ASSERT `s 150: the distance is measured as the Act requires` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 150: the distance is measured as the Act requires` FALSE)

-- s 151 (1): applies to periods of 1 day or longer, for an Act or statutory instrument.
#ASSERT `s 151 (1): s 151 applies in working out the period` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (1): s 151 applies in working out the period` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (1): s 151 applies in working out the period` TRUE FALSE)

-- s 151B (1): applies if something must or may be done, and no time is provided for doing it.
#ASSERT `s 151B (1): s 151B applies to the thing` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151B (1): s 151B applies to the thing` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151B (1): s 151B applies to the thing` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 151B (2): the thing must or may be done as soon as possible and as often as needed.
#ASSERT `s 151B (2): when the thing must or may be done` TRUE EQUALS JUST `as soon as possible and as often as needed`
#ASSERT `s 151B (2): when the thing must or may be done` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 151C (1): applies if something must or may be done on a particular day or within a particular period, and a court or other entity has power to extend the time.
#ASSERT `s 151C (1): s 151C applies to the thing` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151C (1): s 151C applies to the thing` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151C (1): s 151C applies to the thing` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 151C (2), (3): a person may apply, and the court may extend, "even though the relevant time has ended".
#ASSERT `s 151C (2): a person may apply for the relevant time to be extended` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151C (2): a person may apply for the relevant time to be extended` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151C (2): a person may apply for the relevant time to be extended` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151C (3): the court or other entity may extend the relevant time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151C (3): the court or other entity may extend the relevant time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 151C (5) with (6): applies only to an applicable law (enacted after 1 January 2006) or an applicable provision (inserted after it).
#ASSERT `s 151C (5): s 151C applies to the law or provision` (Date 2 1 2006) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151C (5): s 151C applies to the law or provision` (Date 1 1 2006) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 151C (5): s 151C applies to the law or provision` (Date 1 1 2003) (JUST (Date 15 6 2010))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151C (5): s 151C applies to the law or provision` (Date 1 1 2003) (JUST (Date 1 1 2006)))

-- s 152: the obligation to do the act continues until the act is done, even if the period has ended or the person has been convicted.
#ASSERT `s 152: the obligation to do the act continues` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 152: the obligation to do the act continues` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 152: the obligation to do the act continues` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 15.2: Definitions`

-- s 155 (1): "A definition ... applies except so far as the contrary intention appears."
#ASSERT `s 155 (1): the definition applies` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 155 (1): the definition applies` TRUE)

-- s 156 (1) Example 1: the dictionary's signpost definition of x, with nothing in the ABC Act 1999 indicating its intended application, applies to the entire Act.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument` `nothing` EQUALS JUST `the entire Act or instrument`
-- s 156 (1) Example 2: "z, in part 4 (Registration of vehicles), means ..." applies only to part 4.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument` `a more limited application` EQUALS JUST `the more limited part the Act or instrument provides for`
-- s 156 (1) Example 3: the dictionary definition "a—see section 50." applies to the entire Act.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument` `nothing` EQUALS JUST `the entire Act or instrument`
-- s 156 (1) says nothing about a dictionary definition that the Act gives a broader application.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument` `a broader application` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 156 (2) Example 1: the definitions in s 255 (7) apply only to s 255.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in a section of the Act or instrument` `nothing` EQUALS JUST `only the section it is in`
-- s 156 (2) Example 2: "a, for part 6 (Complaints)—see section 50." applies to all of part 6 but not outside it.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument` `a more limited application` EQUALS JUST `the more limited part the Act or instrument provides for`
-- s 156 (2) Example 3: a section beginning "In this Act:" gives its definition a broader application, the entire Act.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in a section of the Act or instrument` `a broader application` EQUALS JUST `the broader part the Act or instrument provides for`
-- s 156 (3) Example: a subsection beginning "In subsection (3):" limits the definition to that subsection.
#ASSERT `s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` `in a section of the Act or instrument` `a more limited application` EQUALS JUST `the more limited part the Act or instrument provides for`
-- s 156 (4): where the Act is divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section is a reference to a corresponding provision.
#ASSERT `s 156 (4): what a reference to a section is a reference to` TRUE EQUALS `the corresponding provision`
#ASSERT `s 156 (4): what a reference to a section is a reference to` FALSE EQUALS `a section`

-- s 157 Example: the Publication (Grants) Act 2001 defines publish, so "published", "publisher", "publishes", "publishing" and "publication" have corresponding meanings.
#ASSERT `s 157: the other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the term have corresponding meanings` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 157: the other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the term have corresponding meanings` FALSE)

§§ `Part 15.3: References to various entities and things`

-- s 160 (1): a reference to a person generally includes a corporation as well as an individual.
#ASSERT `s 160 (1): a reference to a person generally includes the party` `an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160 (1): a reference to a person generally includes the party` `a corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160 (1): a reference to a person generally includes the party` `another kind of party` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 160 (2): subsection (1) is not displaced only because of an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere.
#ASSERT `s 160 (2): subsection (1) is displaced` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 160 (2): subsection (1) is displaced` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 160 Examples—references to a person generally: another person, anyone else, party, someone else, employer.
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "another person" EQUALS JUST `a person generally`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "anyone else" EQUALS JUST `a person generally`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "party" EQUALS JUST `a person generally`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "someone else" EQUALS JUST `a person generally`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "employer" EQUALS JUST `a person generally`
-- s 160 Examples—express references to a corporation: body corporate, company.
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "body corporate" EQUALS JUST `a corporation`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "company" EQUALS JUST `a corporation`
-- s 160 Examples—express references to an individual: adult, child, spouse, driver.
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "adult" EQUALS JUST `an individual`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "child" EQUALS JUST `an individual`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "spouse" EQUALS JUST `an individual`
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "driver" EQUALS JUST `an individual`
-- The examples are not an exhaustive list.
#ASSERT `s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` "tenant" EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 160 (3): "Subsection (2) does not limit the operation of section 6."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 160 (3): subsection (2) limits the operation of section 6`)

-- s 161 (1), (2): a provision creating an offence applies to corporations as well as individuals.
#ASSERT `s 161 (1), (2): a provision of a law that creates an offence applies to the party` `an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161 (1), (2): a provision of a law that creates an offence applies to the party` `a corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161 (1), (2): a provision of a law that creates an offence applies to the party` `another kind of party` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 161 (2) Example: "Maximum penalty: 100 penalty units, imprisonment for 1 year or both." The provision can apply to a corporation.
#ASSERT `s 161 (1), (2): a provision of a law that creates an offence applies to the party` `a corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 161 (3) (a): imprisonment not longer than 6 months, 50 penalty units; both sides of the 6 month threshold.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 6 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST 100
-- s 161 (3) (b): longer than 6 months but not longer than 1 year, 100 penalty units.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 13 EQUALS JUST 200
-- s 161 (3) (c): longer than 1 year but not longer than 2 years, 200 penalty units.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 24 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 25 EQUALS JUST 500
-- s 161 (3) (d): longer than 2 years but not longer than 5 years, 500 penalty units.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 60 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 61 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- s 161 (3) (e): longer than 5 years but not longer than 10 years, 1 000 penalty units.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 120 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- s 161 (3) (f): longer than 10 years, 1 500 penalty units.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 121 EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 600 EQUALS JUST 1500
-- Where the penalty is not imprisonment only, or the corporation is not convicted, s 161 (3) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE FALSE 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` FALSE TRUE 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 161 (4): law means an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` `a subordinate law`
#ASSERT `s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` `a disallowable instrument`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` `a notifiable instrument`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` `a commencement notice`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` `a statutory instrument of another kind`)

GIVETH A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
`one Minister administers` MEANS
    `Who administers or is responsible for a provision` WITH
        `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision` IS LIST "Minister A"
        `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters` IS FALSE
        `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
`two Ministers administer` MEANS
    `Who administers or is responsible for a provision` WITH
        `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision` IS LIST "Minister A", "Minister B"
        `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters` IS FALSE
        `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
`different Ministers for different matters, one for the relevant matter` MEANS
    `Who administers or is responsible for a provision` WITH
        `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision` IS LIST "Minister A", "Minister B"
        `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters` IS TRUE
        `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter` IS LIST "Minister B"

GIVETH A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
`different Ministers for different matters, two for the relevant matter` MEANS
    `Who administers or is responsible for a provision` WITH
        `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision` IS LIST "Minister A", "Minister B", "Minister C"
        `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters` IS TRUE
        `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter` IS LIST "Minister B", "Minister C"

GIVETH A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
`nobody administers` MEANS
    `Who administers or is responsible for a provision` WITH
        `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision` IS EMPTY
        `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters` IS FALSE
        `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter` IS EMPTY

-- s 162 (2) (a): the Minister for the time being administering the provision.
#ASSERT `s 162 (2): who a reference to the Minister without a title is a reference to` `one Minister administers` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister A"), `any one of them` IS FALSE)
-- s 162 (2) (c): if (b) does not apply and 2 or more Ministers administer the provision, any of the Ministers.
#ASSERT `s 162 (2): who a reference to the Minister without a title is a reference to` `two Ministers administer` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister A", "Minister B"), `any one of them` IS TRUE)
-- s 162 (2) (b) (i): different Ministers for different matters, only 1 for the relevant matter, the Minister.
#ASSERT `s 162 (2): who a reference to the Minister without a title is a reference to` `different Ministers for different matters, one for the relevant matter` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister B"), `any one of them` IS FALSE)
-- s 162 (2) (b) (ii): 2 or more for the relevant matter, any of the Ministers.
#ASSERT `s 162 (2): who a reference to the Minister without a title is a reference to` `different Ministers for different matters, two for the relevant matter` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister B", "Minister C"), `any one of them` IS TRUE)
-- No Minister administers the provision: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `s 162 (2): who a reference to the Minister without a title is a reference to` `nobody administers` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 163 (2) has the same three limbs for administrative units.
#ASSERT `s 163 (2): which administrative unit's director-general a reference to the director-general without a title is a reference to` `one Minister administers` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister A"), `any one of them` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 163 (2): which administrative unit's director-general a reference to the director-general without a title is a reference to` `two Ministers administer` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister A", "Minister B"), `any one of them` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 163 (2): which administrative unit's director-general a reference to the director-general without a title is a reference to` `different Ministers for different matters, two for the relevant matter` EQUALS JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS (LIST "Minister B", "Minister C"), `any one of them` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 163 (2): which administrative unit's director-general a reference to the director-general without a title is a reference to` `nobody administers` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 162 (1): a Minister is the Chief Minister or a Minister appointed under the Self-Government Act, section 41.
#ASSERT `s 162 (1): the person is a Minister` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 162 (1): the person is a Minister` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162 (1): the person is a Minister` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 162 (3): "Minister includes a Minister for the time being acting on behalf of the Minister or 2 or more Ministers."
#ASSERT `s 162 (3): the reference to the Minister in subsection (2) includes the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 162 (3): the reference to the Minister in subsection (2) includes the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 162 (4) and s 163 (3): where the Act identifies the Minister (or director-general) by a stated Act, instrument or provision, that decides it.
#ASSERT `s 162 (4): the provision whose administration decides which Minister the reference is to` "s 10" (JUST "the Xyz Act 2001") EQUALS "the Xyz Act 2001"
#ASSERT `s 162 (4): the provision whose administration decides which Minister the reference is to` "s 10" NOTHING EQUALS "s 10"
#ASSERT `s 163 (3): the provision whose responsibility decides which director-general the reference is to` "s 10" (JUST "the Xyz Act 2001") EQUALS "the Xyz Act 2001"
#ASSERT `s 163 (3): the provision whose responsibility decides which director-general the reference is to` "s 10" NOTHING EQUALS "s 10"
-- s 163 (1): a director-general is a person employed under the Public Sector Management Act, section 31, to perform the duties of an office of director-general.
#ASSERT `s 163 (1): the person is a director-general` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 163 (1): the person is a director-general` FALSE)

-- s 164 (1): 'Australian Standard' or 'AS' followed by a number: Standards Australia.
#ASSERT `s 164 (1), (2): the publisher of the standard a reference names` "Australian Standard" EQUALS JUST `Standards Australia`
#ASSERT `s 164 (1), (2): the publisher of the standard a reference names` "AS" EQUALS JUST `Standards Australia`
-- s 164 (2): 'Australian/New Zealand Standard' or 'AS/NZS' followed by a number: Standards Australia and Standards New Zealand jointly.
#ASSERT `s 164 (1), (2): the publisher of the standard a reference names` "Australian/New Zealand Standard" EQUALS JUST `Standards Australia and Standards New Zealand, jointly`
#ASSERT `s 164 (1), (2): the publisher of the standard a reference names` "AS/NZS" EQUALS JUST `Standards Australia and Standards New Zealand, jointly`
#ASSERT `s 164 (1), (2): the publisher of the standard a reference names` "ISO" EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 165: a committee that no longer exists is replaced by the committee nominated by the Speaker.
#ASSERT `s 165: the committee a reference to a committee that no longer exists is a reference to` TRUE (JUST "the Standing Committee on Planning") EQUALS JUST "the Standing Committee on Planning"
#ASSERT `s 165: the committee a reference to a committee that no longer exists is a reference to` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165: the committee a reference to a committee that no longer exists is a reference to` FALSE (JUST "the Standing Committee on Planning") EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land includes the person's personal representatives, successors and assigns.
#ASSERT `s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes the person` `the person with the interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes the person` `the person's personal representative` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes the person` `the person's successor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes the person` `the person's assign` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes the person` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 168 Examples—references to people with interests in land: proprietor, transferor or transferee, mortgagor or mortgagee, lessor or lessee, sublessor or sublessee, trustee.
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "proprietor" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "transferor or transferee" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "mortgagor or mortgagee" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "lessor or lessee" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "sublessor or sublessee" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "trustee" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` "neighbour" EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 169 (1): a person's domestic partner is someone who lives with the person in a domestic partnership, and includes a spouse, civil union partner or civil partner.
#ASSERT `s 169 (1): a reference to a person's domestic partner includes the relationship` `someone who lives with the person in a domestic partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (1): a reference to a person's domestic partner includes the relationship` `a spouse of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (1): a reference to a person's domestic partner includes the relationship` `a civil union partner of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (1): a reference to a person's domestic partner includes the relationship` `a civil partner of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (1): a reference to a person's domestic partner includes the relationship` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 169 (2): a domestic partnership is the relationship between 2 people living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis.
#ASSERT `s 169 (2): the relationship between the two people is a domestic partnership` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 169 (2): the relationship between the two people is a domestic partnership` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 169 (2): the relationship between the two people is a domestic partnership` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 169 (2) Example—indicators: the first is "the length of their relationship", the last is "the reputation, and public aspects, of the relationship between them", and there are ten.
#ASSERT elem "the length of their relationship" `s 169 (2), example: the indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership`
#ASSERT elem "whether they are living together" `s 169 (2), example: the indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership`
#ASSERT elem "the reputation, and public aspects, of the relationship between them" `s 169 (2), example: the indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership`
#ASSERT NOT (elem "the colour of their front door" `s 169 (2), example: the indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership`)
-- s 169 (3): a reference to a domestic partnership includes a marriage, a civil union and a civil partnership.
#ASSERT `s 169 (3): a reference to a domestic partnership includes the relationship` `a marriage` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (3): a reference to a domestic partnership includes the relationship` `a civil union` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (3): a reference to a domestic partnership includes the relationship` `a civil partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169 (3): a reference to a domestic partnership includes the relationship` `another relationship` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 169A (1): a transgender person identifies as a member of a different sex by living, or seeking to live, as a member of that sex, or has identified as one by living as a member of that sex.
#ASSERT `s 169A (1): the person is a transgender person` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 169A (1): the person is a transgender person` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 169A (1): the person is a transgender person` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 169A (2): includes a person who is thought of as a transgender person.
#ASSERT `s 169A (2): a transgender person includes the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 169A (2): a transgender person includes the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 169A (3): a recognised transgender person is a person the record of whose sex is altered under the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1997, part 4 or a corresponding law.
#ASSERT `s 169A (3): the person is a recognised transgender person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 169A (3): the person is a recognised transgender person` FALSE)
-- s 169B: an intersex person has physical, hormonal or genetic features that are (a) not fully female or fully male, (b) a combination of male or female, or (c) not female or male.
#ASSERT `s 169B: the person is an intersex person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 169B: the person is an intersex person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 169B: the person is an intersex person` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
