§§ `Part 15.4: Preservation of certain common law privileges`

-- s 170 (1): an Act or statutory instrument must be interpreted to preserve the privileges.
#ASSERT `s 170 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privileges against self-incrimination and exposure to the imposition of a civil penalty` `an Act (including this Act)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 170 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privileges against self-incrimination and exposure to the imposition of a civil penalty` `a statutory instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 170 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privileges against self-incrimination and exposure to the imposition of a civil penalty` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 170 (2): "However, this section does not affect the operation of the Evidence Act 2011."
#ASSERT `s 170 (2): this section affects the operation of the Evidence Act 2011` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 171 (1), (2): the same for client legal privilege.
#ASSERT `s 171 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privilege in relation to client legal privilege` `an Act (including this Act)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privilege in relation to client legal privilege` `a statutory instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privilege in relation to client legal privilege` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171 (2): this section affects the operation of the Evidence Act 2011` EQUALS JUST FALSE
